om/users/shirakaba/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shirakaba/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shirakaba/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shirakaba/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shirakaba/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shirakaba/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shirakaba/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-06-04T11:00:03Z","updated_at":"2021-06-04T11:04:04Z","body":"I don't think this is a Tauri-specific issue, but I decided to try it just through a local Apache web server using Safari 14.1.1 on macOS 10.15.7 out of interest.\r\n\r\nI made only three changes to your https://github.com/olegshilov/tauri-testing/tree/iframe-issue/app:\r\n\r\n* In `index.html`, I changed the start of each path from `/iframe.html` to `./iframe.html` (because I was in a subdirectory of the web server).\r\n* I added the HTML to `iframe.html` to print out the URLs:\r\n    ```html\r\n    <p>location.href: <span id=\"loc\"></span></p>\r\n    <script>document.getElementById(\"loc\").textContent = location.href</script>\r\n    ```\r\n* In `index.html`, I also increased the iframe width to 500 to see the full URL:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1367\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/14055146/120791266-e3243a80-c52b-11eb-9687-6998829289aa.png\">\r\n\r\nCuriously it works fully over Apache. Can't immediately explain why it's behaving different in the Tauri context.\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tauri-apps/tauri/issues/comments/854617572/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"shirakaba","id":14055146,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MDU1MTQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.g